      "change": "GLM-4.7 pinned to a single upstream provider (Google), allow_fallbacks disabled",
      "reason": "OpenRouter fans z-ai/glm-4.7 across eight upstream providers at fp4, fp8, fp16 and unknown quantization. Under default routing ~90% of calls returned null content with finish_reason=stop after ~141 tokens (Venice) or exhausted the token cap inside the reasoning trace (AtlasCloud). Sampled success: Z.AI 3/3, Google 3/3, DeepInfra 0/3. Pinning holds provider and quantization constant across both decoding arms, which the contrast requires; the unpinned mixture does not. Google chosen over the first-party Z.AI route on cost, with the remaining balance at $3.78 and Z.AI projecting $3.89.",
      "discarded": "28 GLM generations collected under mixed routing, archived at analysis/smoke_archive/glm_mixed_routing_2026-08-03.jsonl",
      "affects": "GLM-4.7 only; the other three endpoints completed 360/360 per arm under default routing"
    }
